 183:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c **** 
 184:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c **** /**
 185:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****    * @brief  Update SystemCoreClock variable according to Clock Register Values.
 186:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         The SystemCoreClock variable contains the core clock (HCLK), it can
 187:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         be used by the user application to setup the SysTick timer or configure
 188:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         other parameters.
 189:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           
 190:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   * @note   Each time the core clock (HCLK) changes, this function must be called
 191:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         to update SystemCoreClock variable value. Otherwise, any configuration
 192:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         based on this variable will be incorrect.         
 193:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *     
 194:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   * @note   - The system frequency computed by this function is not the real 
 195:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           frequency in the chip. It is calculated based on the predefined 
 196:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           constant and the selected clock source:
 197:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *             
 198:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSI, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSI_VALUE(*)
 199:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *                                              
 200:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is HSE, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**)
 201:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *                          
 202:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *           - If SYSCLK source is PLL, SystemCoreClock will contain the HSE_VALUE(**) 
 203:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *             or HSI_VALUE(*) multiplied/divided by the PLL factors.
 204:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         
 205:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         (*) HSI_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32f4xx_hal_conf.h file (default value
 206:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *             16 MHz) but the real value may vary depending on the variations
 207:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *             in voltage and temperature.   
 208:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *    
 209:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *         (**) HSE_VALUE is a constant defined in stm32f4xx_hal_conf.h file (its value
 210:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *              depends on the application requirements), user has to ensure that HSE_VALUE
 211:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *              is same as the real frequency of the crystal used. Otherwise, this function
 212:../system/src/cmsis/system_stm32f4xx.c ****   *              may have wrong result.
